    {
     "id": "content_block_1776744740718_dwoqb1p7t",
     "type": "content_block",
     "variant": "content-block-21-pro",
     "name": "FAQ",
     "anchor": {
      "enabled": true,
      "name": "Printing Tips",
      "id": "content_block_1776744740718_dwoqb1p7t"
     },
     "modules": {
      "typeStyles": {
       "content": {
        "title": "Printing Tips"
       }
      },
      "featureConfig": {
       "faqs": [
        {
         "question": "1.Accessory Compatibility",
         "answerBlocks": [
          {
           "type": "rich-text",
           "content": "<div>Not compatible with <strong>Hotend with Stainless Steel Nozzle 0.2 mm</strong>.</div>",
           "id": "comp_1789728488296_dsvkwg9cv"
          }
         ],
         "id": "comp_1789728488296_4bmlva19h"
        },
        {
         "question": "2.Drying Recommendations",
         "answerBlocks": [
          {
           "type": "rich-text",
           "content": "<div>Dry before use to ensure the best print quality and consistent finish. Store in a dry environment after use. For more details, please refer to: <a href=\"https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/filament-acc/filament/dry-filament\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42; text-decoration: underline;\">Filament drying instructions</span></span></a> on WIKI.</div>",
           "id": "comp_1789728488296_zk5i4xsy3"
          }
         ],
         "id": "comp_1789728488296_d3ll5diie"
        },
        {
         "question": "3.Appearance Change",
         "answerBlocks": [
          {
           "type": "rich-text",
           "content": "<ul>\n<li>Please note that the transparency of prints may vary depending on factors such as size, thickness, structure, and printing parameters (including speed, nozzle temperature, and infill density). To enhance translucency, please refer to the <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\"><span style=\"color: #00ae42; text-decoration: underline;\"><a style=\"color: #00ae42; text-decoration: underline;\" href=\"https://wiki.bambulab.com/en/knowledge-sharing/transparent-petg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">printing tips</a></span></span> on WIKI.</li>\n</ul>",
           "id": "comp_1789728488296_4zps64abg"
          },
          {
           "type": "rich-text",
           "content": "<ul>\n<li>PLA Translucent has a frosted glass texture that diffuses light well, while PETG Translucent is more see-through with a crystal-clear finish.</li>\n</ul>",
           "id": "comp_1789728488296_m1v6efovp"
          },
          {
           "type": "media",
           "media": {
            "pc": {
             "type": "image",
             "src": "https://store.bblcdn.com/s7/default/12aed21ae43b414b9b3fb5b4b25b7b31/Bambu_PLA_Translucent07-compressed.jpg",
             "naturalWidth": 1992,
             "naturalHeight": 480
            },
            "mo": {
             "type": "image",
             "src": "https://store.bblcdn.com/s7/default/e05848a83ffd4f4c8e18c39f795d6949/Bambu_PLA_Translucent_MO10-compressed.jpg",
             "naturalWidth": 1344,
             "naturalHeight": 960
            }
           },
           "id": "comp_1789728488296_ctmxrg9uw"
          }
         ],
         "id": "comp_1789728488296_m8g9h29sq"
        },
        {
         "question": "4.Printability",
         "answerBlocks": [
          {
           "type": "rich-text",
           "content": "<div>PLA Translucent is more beginner-friendly than PETG Translucent.</div>",
           "id": "comp_1789728488296_jzpml26j2"
          }
         ],
         "id": "comp_1789728488296_jfem1pp28"
        },
        {
         "question": "5.Safety Tips",
         "answerBlocks": [
          {
           "type": "rich-text",
           "content": "<ul>\n<li>Please store the filament in a cool, dark, and dry environment away from direct sunlight and high temperatures.</li>\n<li>Please keep filament and any broken fragments out of reach of infants, children, and pets to prevent swallowing or choking.</li>\n<li>For opened filament, we recommend drying before use according to the wiki&rsquo;s recommended temperature and time settings.</li>\n<li>Please print this filament in a well-ventilated area, or install an effective air filtration or exhaust system.</li>\n<li>As this filament is not food-grade, please avoid using finished prints for food storage or contact.&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>",
           "id": "comp_1789728488296_5gp7bxpvl"
          }
         ],
         "id": "comp_1789728488296_hg1i0trm6"
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    }
   ]
  }
